.TH MERKADU 1 "October 2026" "SDE" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
merkadu \- the SDE software center: find, install and remove apps
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B merkadu
[\fB--page\fR \fINAME\fR] [\fB--search\fR \fITEXT\fR] [\fB--category\fR \fIID\fR]
[\fB--details\fR \fIAPPID\fR]
.br
.B merkadu
\fBappstream://\fIAPPID\fR
.br
.B merkadu
\fB--uninstall\fR \fIFILE\fB.desktop\fR
.br
.B merkadu
\fB--version\fR | \fB--help\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBMerkadu\fR is the software center of the Selviana Desktop Environment. It
finds, installs, updates and removes apps from three sources:
.TP
.B Debian
the packages of the system's APT sources, through PackageKit, described by
the AppStream catalog of the archive (\fI/usr/share/swcatalog\fR).
.TP
.B Flatpak
apps of the Flatpak remotes of the system installation (and those installed
for the user), with libflatpak. When Flatpak has no Flathub remote, the
Sources page offers to add it.
.TP
.B Snap
the Snap Store, through snapd's REST API on \fI/run/snapd.socket\fR. The
source appears when snapd is installed and running.
.PP
One search covers every source. An app that more than one source offers is
shown once, with a badge per source; its page lets you choose the source to
install from and shows the version, size, license and isolation of each.
.PP
The window has a sidebar with \fBExplore\fR (featured apps, new and updated
apps, top apps and the departments), \fBInstalled\fR (grouped by department),
\fBUpdates\fR (app updates; system updates belong to Software Updater,
\fBsde-update\fR(1)), \fBHistory\fR (installations, updates and removals of
every source, by day), \fBIn Progress\fR (the queue of changes, with the
animated SDE logo) and \fBSources\fR. The departments and their
subcategories come from Ubuntu Software Center, on which Merkadu is based.
.PP
Installing, updating and removing ask for authorization with polkit (the SDE
authentication dialog): PackageKit for Debian packages, the Flatpak system
helper for the system installation and snapd for snaps. Merkadu itself runs
as the user and never as root.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --page " NAME"
open a page: \fBexplore\fR, \fBinstalled\fR, \fBupdates\fR, \fBhistory\fR,
\fBprogress\fR or \fBsources\fR.
.TP
.BI --search " TEXT"
search for \fITEXT\fR.
.TP
.BI --category " ID"
open a department, such as \fBgames\fR or \fBgraphics/photography\fR.
.TP
.BI --details " APPID"
open the page of an app: its AppStream id (\fBorg.gimp.GIMP\fR), or
\fBdeb:\fIPACKAGE\fR, \fBflatpak:\fIREF\fR or \fBsnap:\fINAME\fR.
.TP
.BI appstream:// APPID
the same as \fB--details\fR; Merkadu handles the \fBappstream:\fR links of
app websites.
.TP
.BI --uninstall " FILE"
uninstall the app of a launcher, given the absolute path of its
\fI.desktop\fR file (the Start menu's \fBUninstall\fR). A small window shows
the app's icon and name, where it comes from (the Debian package that owns
the file, the Flatpak of \fBX-Flatpak=\fR or the snap of
\fBX-SnapInstanceName=\fR), the disk space it frees and the other packages
that are removed with it, and asks before removing it. A launcher in the
user's home that no package installed is removed on its own. Apps of SDE's
own packages (\fBsde\fR, \fBsde-desktop\fR, \fBmerkadu\fR) are not removed on
their own, and neither is an app whose removal would take one of them away.
.TP
.B --version
print the version and exit.
.TP
.B --help
print the usage and exit.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B Ctrl+F, Ctrl+K
search.
.TP
.B Alt+Left, Backspace, Escape
back.
.TP
.B F5
reload the sources.
.TP
.B F1
about Merkadu.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Q
quit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
With \fB--uninstall\fR: \fB0\fR when the app was removed, \fB1\fR when it
could not be removed or Merkadu refused to remove it, \fB2\fR when the user
cancelled. Otherwise \fB0\fR, or \fB2\fR for a wrong command line.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/merkadu/merkadu.conf
the defaults: featured and top apps of the lobby, the number of new apps,
the order of the sources, the Flathub repository file, whether to hide the
snap folder and more protected packages. Distributions override it with
\fI/etc/merkadu/merkadu.conf\fR or a file in
\fI$XDG_CONFIG_DIRS/merkadu/\fR.
.TP
.I /usr/share/merkadu/categories.menu
the departments (Ubuntu Software Center's menu format); files in
\fI/usr/share/merkadu/menu.d/\fR and \fI/etc/merkadu/menu.d/\fR add or
replace departments.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/merkadu/images
downloaded icons and screenshots.
.TP
.I /var/log/apt/history.log
the history of Debian packages; Flatpak's comes from \fBflatpak history\fR
and the Snap history from snapd's changes.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MERKADU_CONFIG
a configuration file used instead of the ones above.
.TP
.B MERKADU_FAKE
a directory with a fake catalog (\fIcatalog.json\fR): all three sources are
simulated, nothing is installed or downloaded. For tests and screenshots.
.SH NOTES
snapd keeps each user's snap data in \fI~/snap\fR. Before the first snap is
installed, Merkadu sets snapd's \fBexperimental.hidden-snap-folder\fR option,
which moves it to \fI~/.snap/data\fR; snapd cannot keep it outside the home
folder. See \fI/usr/share/doc/merkadu/MERKADU.md\fR.
